  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1 DESCRIPTION...\n\nAreas of dense fog are possible early this morning, affecting\nthe morning commute. The fog should thin out by 9 am most areas\nexcept perhaps the immediate coast and deeper valleys.\n\nScattered showers are then possible this afternoon as cool\ncyclonic flow aloft persists along with weak SFC troffing. \nHighs should be warmer today with lesser clouds, especially in \nthe morning.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2 DESCRIPTION...\n\nA mid-level trough deepens over the Canadian Maritimes on Saturday. \nA surface low looks to stall over Nova Scotia, allowing for the \ndevelopment of some retrograding showers along a backdoor cold front \nSaturday. A few rumbles of thunder can't be ruled out Saturday \nnight. Temperatures Saturday may trend downward on the coastal \nplain during the afternoon. By Sunday evening, the \naforementioned surface low over Nova Scotia is expected to shift\nto the southeast with high pressure moving in. High pressure \nwill allow for tranquil weather for most of Monday/Labor Day. \nPersistent northerly flow over the weekend will lead to cooler \ntemperatures and dewpoints through the holiday weekend with \nhighs mainly in the lower 70s and some breezier winds out of the\nnorth. Unsettled and warmer weather may return towards the \nmiddle of next week.",
